    "term": "First Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  In John 8:12 and 9:5, Jesus declares <em>'I am the light of the world.'</em> This powerful <span class=\"learn-keyword\">'I AM'</span> statement reveals Jesus as the source of spiritual illumination, truth, and life for all humanity. Understanding this title helps believers live in the light and share it with others.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. The Declaration (John 8:12)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Jesus said: <em>'I am the light of the world. Whoever follows me will never walk in darkness, but will have the light of life.'</em> This was spoken during the Feast of Tabernacles in Jerusalem, when large golden lampstands lit the temple courts. Jesus was claiming to be the true, eternal light that those lamps symbolised.</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>The context: the woman caught in adultery (John 8:1–11) immediately preceded this declaration.</li>\n  <li>Jesus contrasts His light with the spiritual darkness of sin and ignorance.</li>\n  <li>The promise: followers 'will have the light of life' — both guidance now and eternal life.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. A Second Declaration (John 9:5)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">As Jesus healed the man born blind, He said: <em>'While I am in the world, I am the light of the world.'</em> This healing was a sign — physical blindness being cured was a picture of spiritual blindness being cured by Jesus. The Pharisees who could see physically were shown to be spiritually blind (John 9:40–41).</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Meaning and Significance</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>What Light Does</th><th>What Jesus Does</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Dispels darkness</td><td>Overcomes sin and evil (John 1:5)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Guides the way</td><td>Guides believers through life (Psalm 119:105)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Reveals what is hidden</td><td>Exposes sin and reveals truth (John 3:19–21)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sustains life</td><td>Gives eternal life to those who follow</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Believers as Light</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">In Matthew 5:14, Jesus tells His disciples: <em>'You are the light of the world.'</em> Believers reflect Christ's light to others — through righteous living, sharing the gospel, and acts of love.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Key Verses:</strong> John 8:12 (at Feast of Tabernacles); John 9:5 (healing of blind man); John 1:4–5, 9; Matthew 5:14–16.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Jesus declared 'I am the light of the world' twice (John 8:12; 9:5). Light dispels darkness, guides, reveals truth, and sustains life — all things Jesus does spiritually. The healing of the blind man (John 9) illustrates spiritual illumination. Believers are also light (Matthew 5:14), reflecting Christ.\n</div>\n  ",
