    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Sonship</span> describes the relationship of believers with God as His children. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">John 1:12</span> says: <em>'Yet to all who received him, to those who believed in his name, he gave the right to become children of God.'</em> <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Romans 8:14–17</span> deepens this, explaining what it means to live as God's children through the Spirit.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. How Believers Become Children of God (John 1:12)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Sonship is not natural — it is received by grace through faith:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>'Received him'</strong> — accepted Jesus as Lord and Saviour.</li>\n  <li><strong>'Believed in his name'</strong> — trusted in His person, character, and work.</li>\n  <li><strong>'Right (authority) to become children'</strong> — a legal right granted by God.</li>\n  <li>Note: John 1:13 clarifies this is 'not of natural descent, nor of human decision... but born of God.'</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. The Spirit of Adoption (Romans 8:14–17)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><em>'Those who are led by the Spirit of God are the children of God. The Spirit you received does not make you slaves, so that you live in fear again; rather, the Spirit you received brought about your adoption to sonship. And by him we cry, \"Abba, Father.\"'</em></p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Led by the Spirit</strong> = evidence of sonship (v.14).</li>\n  <li><strong>Spirit of adoption</strong> — not a spirit of fear/slavery but of closeness (v.15).</li>\n  <li><strong>'Abba, Father'</strong> — intimate, personal address (like 'Daddy') — Jesus used this in Gethsemane (Mark 14:36).</li>\n  <li><strong>Co-heirs with Christ</strong> — sharing Christ's inheritance, if we also share His suffering (v.17).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Privileges and Responsibilities of Sonship</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Privileges</th><th>Responsibilities</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Access to God as Father</td><td>Obedience and holiness</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Inheritance with Christ</td><td>Following the Spirit's lead</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>God's care and provision</td><td>Loving others as brothers and sisters</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Eternal security</td><td>Bearing the family likeness (Matthew 5:45)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Key Verse:</strong> Romans 8:15 — 'The Spirit you received brought about your adoption to sonship. And by him we cry, \"Abba, Father.\"'\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Sonship begins by receiving and believing in Jesus (John 1:12). The Holy Spirit confirms our adoption and enables intimate prayer (Abba — Romans 8:15). Believers are co-heirs with Christ (Romans 8:17). Sonship involves both privilege (inheritance, access, care) and responsibility (led by Spirit, holy living, loving others).\n</div>\n  ",
