    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Galatians 5:22–23</span> lists the ninefold fruit of the Spirit: <em>'love, joy, peace, forbearance (patience), kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness and self-control.'</em> This fruit describes the character of Christ being formed in the believer by the Holy Spirit — the natural result of abiding in Christ (John 15:4–5).\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. What is the Fruit of the Spirit?</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Unlike spiritual gifts (which are given selectively), the fruit of the Spirit is the <strong>whole character of Christ</strong> produced in every believer who walks in the Spirit. It is singular ('fruit,' not 'fruits') — one unified cluster of qualities, not separate achievements.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. The Ninefold Fruit</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Fruit</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Love (agape)</td><td>Unconditional, self-giving love for God and others</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Joy</td><td>Deep, settled gladness independent of circumstances</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Peace</td><td>Wholeness, harmony; absence of inner turmoil</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Patience (forbearance)</td><td>Long-suffering endurance under provocation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Kindness</td><td>Gentle goodness toward others in practical ways</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Goodness</td><td>Moral excellence; active righteousness</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Faithfulness</td><td>Trustworthiness, reliability, loyalty</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Gentleness (meekness)</td><td>Strength under control; humility</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Self-control</td><td>Mastery of one's desires, passions, and impulses</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. How the Fruit Grows</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Galatians 5:16–18 explains: 'Walk by the Spirit and you will not gratify the desires of the flesh.' The fruit grows as believers:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Abide in Christ (John 15:4–5)</li>\n  <li>Yield to the Spirit rather than the flesh</li>\n  <li>Are transformed by renewing their minds (Romans 12:2)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Contrast:</strong> Galatians 5:19–21 lists the works of the flesh (sexual immorality, idolatry, hatred, discord, etc.) in contrast to the fruit of the Spirit. The question for every believer is: which is growing?\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> The fruit of the Spirit (Galatians 5:22–23) is Christ's character produced by the Holy Spirit in the believer. It is a unity (one fruit), not a selection. Love heads the list. Grown by abiding in Christ and walking by the Spirit. Contrasted with the works of the flesh.\n</div>\n  ",
