    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">1 Corinthians 12</span> and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Romans 12:6–8</span> describe spiritual gifts — special abilities given by the Holy Spirit to believers for building up the Church. Unlike the fruit of the Spirit (which every believer should have), gifts are distributed selectively 'just as he determines' (1 Corinthians 12:11).\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. What are Spiritual Gifts?</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Spiritual gifts (Greek: charismata = grace-gifts) are God-given abilities for ministry and service. They are:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Given by the <strong>Holy Spirit</strong>, not earned by human achievement.</li>\n  <li>For the <strong>common good</strong> — to benefit the whole body of Christ (1 Corinthians 12:7).</li>\n  <li>Distributed <strong>as the Spirit wills</strong> — not by human choice (1 Corinthians 12:11).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Categories of Gifts (1 Corinthians 12:8–10, 28–30; Romans 12:6–8)</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Gifts</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Speaking gifts</td><td>Prophecy, tongues, interpretation, teaching, encouragement</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Service gifts</td><td>Service/helps, leadership, giving, mercy</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sign gifts</td><td>Healing, miracles, distinguishing spirits, faith</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Knowledge gifts</td><td>Wisdom, knowledge, discernment</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. The Body Analogy (1 Corinthians 12:12–27)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Paul compares the Church to a human body: many members with different functions, but one body. No member should say 'I don't belong' (feeling inferior) nor 'I don't need you' (feeling superior). Every gift is essential.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. The Purpose of Gifts</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Ephesians 4:12–13 — gifts are given 'to equip his people for works of service, so that the body of Christ may be built up until we all reach unity in the faith and in the knowledge of the Son of God.'</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Key Principle:</strong> 1 Corinthians 12:7 — 'To each one the manifestation of the Spirit is given for the common good.' Gifts are for others, not for self-promotion.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Spiritual gifts are grace-given abilities for ministry (charismata). Given by the Spirit, distributed selectively, for the common good of the Church. Body analogy: diversity in unity. No gift is superior; all are essential. Purpose: equipping believers for service and building up the Body of Christ.\n</div>\n  ",
