    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Acts 1:8</span> records Jesus's final commission: <em>'But you will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes on you; and you will be my witnesses in Jerusalem, and in all Judea and Samaria, and to the ends of the earth.'</em> Witnessing is not optional — every believer is called to share the good news of Christ by word and by life.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. The Great Commission (Matthew 28:18–20)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Before His ascension, Jesus commanded: <em>'Go and make disciples of all nations, baptising them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, and teaching them to obey everything I have commanded you.'</em></p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Authority:</strong> 'All authority in heaven and earth has been given to me' — the commission is backed by supreme authority.</li>\n  <li><strong>Scope:</strong> 'All nations' — witnessing crosses every cultural, linguistic, and geographical boundary.</li>\n  <li><strong>Content:</strong> 'Teaching them to obey' — discipleship, not just conversion.</li>\n  <li><strong>Promise:</strong> 'I am with you always, to the very end of the age.'</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. The Power for Witnessing (Acts 1:8)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The Holy Spirit is the power behind effective witnessing — not human eloquence or strategy. The early Church received the Spirit at Pentecost (Acts 2) and immediately began witnessing boldly.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Methods of Witnessing</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Verbal testimony</td><td>Sharing your personal story of coming to faith</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Life witness</td><td>Righteous, loving, honest living (Matthew 5:16)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Good deeds</td><td>Acts of service and compassion (James 2:17)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Inviting others</td><td>Bringing people to church or Bible study</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Jerusalem, Judea, Samaria, Ends of the Earth</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Acts 1:8 outlines a geographical progression — from home (Jerusalem = your immediate community) to your region (Judea), to cultural boundaries (Samaria), to the whole world. Witnessing starts where you are.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Key Verse:</strong> Acts 1:8 — 'You will receive power when the Holy Spirit comes on you; and you will be my witnesses.' Witnessing requires the Holy Spirit's power, not just human effort.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Every believer is a witness (Acts 1:8). The Great Commission (Matthew 28:18–20) calls for making disciples of all nations. Witnessing methods: verbal testimony, life witness, good deeds, invitation. The Holy Spirit provides power. Start where you are (Jerusalem) and expand outward.\n</div>\n  ",
