    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This topic builds on Witnessing I by examining the cost and courage of witnessing, the role of suffering in testimony, and the importance of consistent daily witness through a transformed life. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">2 Timothy 4:1–5</span> and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">1 Peter 3:13–17</span> are key passages.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. The Cost of Witnessing</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Jesus warned: <em>'Everyone who wants to live a godly life in Christ Jesus will be persecuted'</em> (2 Timothy 3:12). Faithful witnessing may bring:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Social rejection or ridicule</li>\n  <li>Family conflict (Matthew 10:34–36)</li>\n  <li>Persecution (Acts 7:54–60 — Stephen)</li>\n  <li>Imprisonment (Acts 16:22–34 — Paul and Silas)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. The Call to Courage (2 Timothy 4:1–5)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Paul charges Timothy: <em>'Preach the word; be prepared in season and out of season; correct, rebuke and encourage — with great patience and careful instruction... keep your head in all situations, endure hardship, do the work of an evangelist, discharge all the duties of your ministry.'</em></p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Witnessing Under Pressure (1 Peter 3:13–17)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><em>'Always be prepared to give an answer to everyone who asks you to give the reason for the hope that you have. But do this with gentleness and respect, keeping a clear conscience.'</em> (v.15–16)</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Suffering as Witness</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The Greek word for witness is <span class=\"learn-keyword\">martus</span>, from which 'martyr' is derived. Faithful witness under persecution can be the most powerful testimony. Paul and Silas's singing in prison (Acts 16:25) led to the jailer's conversion.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Key Truth:</strong> Witnessing is not dependent on favourable circumstances. Paul wrote letters that spread the gospel from prison. Tertullian said: 'The blood of the martyrs is the seed of the church.'\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Witnessing has a cost (2 Timothy 3:12). Paul charges Timothy to preach 'in season and out of season' (2 Timothy 4:2). Witness with gentleness and respect even under pressure (1 Peter 3:15–16). Paul and Silas's worship in prison (Acts 16:25) was powerful witness. Martyrs' blood has historically spread the church.\n</div>\n  ",
