    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  The <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Second Coming of Christ</span> is one of the most prominent themes in the New Testament — mentioned over 300 times. <span class=\"learn-keyword\">1 Thessalonians 4:13–18</span> and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Matthew 24:36–44</span> describe what will happen and how believers should live in light of it.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. What the Second Coming Involves (1 Thessalonians 4:13–18)</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>The Lord will descend from heaven with a loud command, the voice of the archangel, and the trumpet call of God (v.16).</li>\n  <li>The dead in Christ will rise first (v.16).</li>\n  <li>Then those who are alive will be caught up together with them in the clouds to meet the Lord (v.17).</li>\n  <li>Purpose: 'And so we will be with the Lord forever' (v.17).</li>\n  <li>Application: 'Encourage one another with these words' (v.18).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. The Unknown Hour (Matthew 24:36–44)</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\"><em>'But about that day or hour no one knows, not even the angels in heaven, nor the Son, but only the Father.'</em> (v.36)</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>The coming will be sudden — like a thief in the night (v.43).</li>\n  <li>People will be going about ordinary life — eating, drinking, marrying — when it happens (v.38).</li>\n  <li>The call: <strong>'Therefore keep watch, because you do not know on what day your Lord will come'</strong> (v.42).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Signs of the Second Coming</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Wars and rumours of wars (Matthew 24:6)</li>\n  <li>Famines and earthquakes (Matthew 24:7)</li>\n  <li>Persecution of believers (Matthew 24:9)</li>\n  <li>The gospel preached to all nations (Matthew 24:14)</li>\n  <li>Signs in the sun, moon, and stars (Luke 21:25)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. How to Live in Light of the Second Coming</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Watchfulness:</strong> Matthew 24:42 — 'keep watch'</li>\n  <li><strong>Readiness:</strong> Matthew 24:44 — 'be ready'</li>\n  <li><strong>Faithfulness:</strong> Luke 12:42–44 — serving faithfully</li>\n  <li><strong>Holiness:</strong> 2 Peter 3:11 — 'live holy and godly lives'</li>\n  <li><strong>Encouragement:</strong> 1 Thessalonians 4:18 — encourage one another</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Key Verse:</strong> 1 Thessalonians 4:17 — 'we will be with the Lord forever.' The Second Coming climaxes in eternal union with Christ.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> The Second Coming is certain (Acts 1:11) but its timing is unknown (Matthew 24:36). Events: dead in Christ rise first; living caught up to meet Him (1 Thessalonians 4:16–17). Response: watch, be ready, live faithfully and holily. The Second Coming is a hope and motivation for holy living.\n</div>\n  ",
